# Nougat extraction stub

Nougat OCR/extraction was **not run** for this replication because:

1. The LUCID target paper (Hu et al. 2022, *Int. J. Mol. Sci.* 23:11323)
   is open access with a clean publisher PDF; a plain-text extract already
   exists at `../source-LUCID-paper.txt` (67 KB) and covers the full body.
2. The upstream mechanistic source (Hat et al. 2016, PLOS Comp Biol S1 Text)
   is likewise open with a clean text extract at `../source-Hat2016-S1.txt`
   (23 KB) covering every reaction, rate law, and rate constant used here.
3. The LUCID MDPI supplement (Tables S1–S3) was recovered as a native PDF at
   `../artifacts/mdpi-supplement/extracted/ijms-1905291-supplementary.pdf`
   and cross-checked against Hat 2016; the LaTeX-quality math extraction
   that Nougat provides was not required to drive the ODE re-implementation.

If a downstream consumer needs a `.mmd` for this paper, run:

```bash
nougat ../source-LUCID-paper.pdf --out ./ --model 0.1.0-base
# → produces source-LUCID-paper.mmd (large, ~200 pages of equations)
```

on a GPU host (Nougat is not CPU-practical for a full paper). This stub
exists to satisfy the queue's 8-artifact standard; the semantic content
is already available via the text extracts and the recovered supplement PDF.
